{{ 'ka-diary-entry-review.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  K&A Client Diaries — Entry "Her Review". Docs/client-diaries-
  build-spec.md §3 row B1. Moved directly after the hero per Suraj's
  explicit direction (10 Aug 2026) — a visitor's first priority is
  the client's own verdict, ahead of any narrative/outfit detail.

  Content source: article.excerpt (Shopify's native Excerpt field,
  set in Blog posts editor) — the client's own words, verbatim,
  unedited (spec field 4). Same field also feeds the shorter pulled
  excerpt shown on the Index Featured panel / grid card (see
  sections/ka-diary-featured.liquid). No metafield needed for this
  field — reuses Shopify's own purpose-built field, same reasoning
  as the Journal's dek line (article.excerpt).

  F3 gate: renders nothing at all — not even an empty section shell
  — unless client_diary_consent is explicitly true.

  BUGFIX 2026-08-11: this previously read `article.summary`, which is
  not a real Liquid property on the article object (Shopify's Admin
  GraphQL API calls this field "summary", but the classic Liquid
  `article` drop only exposes it as `excerpt` -- confirmed against
  Shopify's own Liquid reference). `article.summary` silently
  evaluates to blank in Liquid rather than erroring, so this section
  never rendered for any real entry, including Simran's, despite the
  excerpt being correctly set via the Admin API the whole time. Same
  fix applied to sections/ka-diary-featured.liquid and sections/
  ka-article-hero.liquid (Journal dek line), which had the identical
  bug.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign is_consented = false
  if article.metafields.custom.client_diary_consent == true
    assign is_consented = true
  endif
  assign review_text = article.excerpt | strip_html
-%}

{%- if is_consented and review_text != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign occasion_label = 'Client Diary'
    if article.tags contains 'Bridal'
      assign occasion_label = 'Bridal'
    elsif article.tags contains 'Sangeet & Cocktail'
      assign occasion_label = 'Sangeet & Cocktail'
    elsif article.tags contains 'Festive'
      assign occasion_label = 'Festive'
    elsif article.tags contains 'Mother & Family'
      assign occasion_label = 'Mother & Family'
    endif
    assign entry_year = article.metafields.custom.client_diary_year
    if entry_year == blank
      assign entry_year = article.published_at | date: '%Y'
    endif
  -%}
  <section class="e-review" aria-label="Client review">
    <div class="e-review__mark reveal">&ldquo;</div>
    <p class="e-review__quote reveal reveal-delay-1">{{ review_text }}</p>
    <p class="e-review__attr reveal reveal-delay-2">{{ article.title }} &middot; {{ occasion_label }}, {{ entry_year }}</p>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Diary Entry — Her Review",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Reads from the article's native Excerpt field (Shopify Admin → Blog posts → article → Excerpt). Renders nothing unless the entry's consent-to-publish metafield is explicitly set to true."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Diary Entry — Her Review" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
